        <briefdescription>
<para>Assign the arrays the element writes its energy gradients to in every computeKernels() call. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>dElasticEnergy_dQ</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Gradient of the elastic energy, of size <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_elements_1_1_element_1a049378a4baa4433392a7576d7ab4c7f6" kindref="member">Element::getNDofPerElement()</ref>, in the element&apos;s dof order; nullptr, together with <computeroutput>dDissipation_dQ</computeroutput>, stops the output. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>dDissipation_dQ</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Gradient of the dissipation, of the same size and order.</para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
Call it after the material section is assigned. It throws std::invalid_argument if the section or the material cannot provide the gradients, so unsupported setups are rejected before the analysis. The arrays must outlive the assignment. </para>
        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
