    <briefdescription>
<para>Optional capability of an <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_elements_1_1_element" kindref="compound">Element</ref>: the gradients of its elastic energy and dissipation wrt its dofs. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>An element provides the gradients by inheriting from this class next to <ref refid="class_marmot_1_1_discretizations_1_1_elements_1_1_element" kindref="compound">Element</ref>. Frameworks find the capability with <computeroutput>dynamic_cast&lt; EnergyGradientProvider* &gt;( element )</computeroutput>, e.g., for dissipation based arc length control, and assign the output arrays once. The element then writes the gradients in every computeKernels() call, for the state of that call, consistent with its algorithmic update; computeKernelsExplicit() does not write them. Elements without assigned outputs evaluate their kernels as before, and the standard element interface is not affected. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
